        "original_id": "f1d5dde0-6a4c-5353-9845-1f4527413728",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Jesus Jones, The 77s\n- Places: Bradford-on-Avon, Wiltshire\n- People: Michael Roe, Mark Harmon, Bruce Spencer\n- Products: Zeroes and Ones, Perverse\n- Topics: alternative rock, rock bands, singles, albums\n\nFacts:\n- Jesus Jones formed in late 1988 in Bradford-on-Avon in Wiltshire as a British alternative rock band.\n- Jesus Jones recorded and performed from the late 1980s into the 2000s.\n- The 77s are an American rock band.\n- The 77s have included Michael Roe on vocals and guitar, Mark Harmon on bass, and Bruce Spencer on drums.\n- Zeroes and Ones is the third single from Jesus Jones's 1993 album Perverse.\n- Jesus Jones is an English rock group.",
